Daemons, on their own page
=========================

A daemon is either up or it is not, and the only honest way to answer that is to ask — systemd for the
unit state, and a connect attempt on the port. So `/api/quixi/daemons` returns a row per service with
both answers, and the page shows them as one decision: the dot and the label are computed from the same
value, so a row cannot read "inactive" with its light on.

The controls are start, stop and remove. Remove stops the unit, disables it, and *moves the unit file
aside* rather than deleting it — a unit file is a thing somebody wrote, and "Remove" in a window should
not be able to lose it.

Styled from theme variables throughout, so a Core build keeps its own palette; the only fixed colour is
the green that means "running".

